## Location Reminder - Local Configuration Template
## Copy this file to 'local.properties' in the project root on your new machine.
## Do NOT commit 'local.properties' to version control.

# Location of the Android SDK on your machine.
# Android Studio typically generates this automatically when you open the project.
#
# Windows Example:
# sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\<YourUsername>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
#
# macOS Example:
# sdk.dir=/Users/<YourUsername>/Library/Android/sdk
#
# Linux Example:
# sdk.dir=/home/<YourUsername>/Android/Sdk
sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\<YourUsername>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk

## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Optional: Release Signing Configuration
## For building signed release APKs / AABs.
## You can set these here, in ~/.gradle/gradle.properties, or as environment variables.
## Never commit actual credentials or keystore files.
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RELEASE_STORE_FILE=C\:\\path\\to\\your\\release-keystore.jks
# RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=your_store_password_here
# RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=your_key_alias_here
# RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=your_key_password_here

## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Map & Geocoding Notes:
## This project uses MapLibre Native Android SDK with open endpoints:
## - Vector Map Style: OpenFreeMap Bright (https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/bright)
## - Satellite Tiles: Public Esri World Imagery
## - Geocoding: Android Platform Geocoder with OSM Nominatim fallback
## No proprietary API keys (e.g. Google Maps API key) are required to build or run.
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
